<title>USA: FP&amp;L St Lucie 1 nuclear unit at full power.</title>
<headline>FP&amp;L St Lucie 1 nuclear unit at full power.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Florida Power &amp; Light Co's (FP&amp;L) 839-megawatt St Lucie nuclear unit 1 is back to full power after operating at reduced rates since early this month, the company said Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Last night, it returned to full power,&quot; said company spokesman Janice Brady.</p>
<p>The unit was ramped down to around 60 percent power for repairs after a leak was detected in one of the main transformers in the non-nuclear side of the plant.</p>
<p>The St Lucie unit is located on Hutchinson Island, Fla.</p>
<p>- New York Power Desk, + 212 859 1628</p>
</text>
